module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.OrderOfVanishing
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.ConstantGenericStalk

/-!
# The order of vanishing of a meromorphic section along a prime divisor

Let `X` be a locally Noetherian integral scheme, let `L` be a sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules, and let
`ξ ∈ X` be a point of codimension one — the generic point of a prime divisor. Suppose the stalk
`L_ξ` is generated by one element, as it is when `L` is invertible. A meromorphic section `s` of
`L` is, by Tag 01X5, a single element of the stalk `L_η` at the generic point `η` of `X`, and
writing it as `a · s_ξ` for a generator `s_ξ` of `L_ξ` gives a scalar `a` in the function field
`R(X)`. Its order `ord_{𝒪_{X,ξ}}(a)` does not depend on the generator chosen, because two
generators differ by a unit of `𝒪_{X,ξ}`. That integer is the order of vanishing of `s` along
the prime divisor.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.stalkSpecializes_smul`: specialization of stalks of a presheaf of modules
  is semilinear over specialization of stalks of the presheaf of rings.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ordFrac_eq_of_coordinates`: the order of a coordinate of a fixed vector
  with respect to a generator of a cyclic module does not depend on the generator.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.span_germ_eq_top_of_surjective_smul` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.germ_ne_zero_of_injective_smul`: a section of `L` over `U` by which
  multiplication is bijective over every smaller open set has, at each point of `U`, a nonzero
  germ generating the stalk.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_orderOfVanishingData`: the content of Tag 02SF — a meromorphic
  section has a coordinate with respect to some generator of `L_ξ`, and one integer is the
  order of that coordinate for every generator.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.orderOfVanishingData` and `AlgebraicGeometry.orderOfVanishing`: that
  integer, together with its characterization.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_orderOfVanishingData_of_bijective_smul`: the same, with the
  generator replaced by a trivializing section near `ξ`.

## Implementation notes

The meromorphic section enters only through the global section `t` of the constant
generic-stalk module sheaf that Tag 01X5 part (2) attaches to it; `t` is therefore taken as a
parameter rather than produced from a meromorphic section, which both avoids depending on that
comparison isomorphism and makes the statement more general.

The hypothesis that `L_ξ` is cyclic is likewise taken as a parameter — a generator `g` of `L_ξ`
whose image in `L_η` generates `L_η` over `𝒪_{X,η}` and is nonzero. For an invertible sheaf
that is clause 2 of Tag 0B8M. What
`Stacks.InvertibleRankOne.exists_cover_trivialization_of_tensorLeft` produces is exactly the
input of `nonempty_orderOfVanishingData_of_bijective_smul`: a neighbourhood of `ξ` carrying a
section by which multiplication is an isomorphism over that open set and over every smaller
one.

Tag 0B8M, which compares the sheafified invertibility predicate with the presheaf tensor
functor, is available in both directions, and the form this file needs is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_bijective_smul_of_isInvertible`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/InvertibleTrivialization/Basic.lean`), which produces
exactly the hypothesis of `nonempty_orderOfVanishingData_of_bijective_smul`. The parameters
below are therefore dischargeable from `IsInvertible` alone, and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Divisors/OrderOfVanishingInvertible.lean` does so — note
that it must use `Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible` and not the byte-identical
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible`, since only the former carries the 0B8M
trivialization.

The independence of the order from the generator is isolated as a statement of commutative
algebra: `ordFrac_eq_of_coordinates` works with a semilinear map `M →ₛₗ[algebraMap R K] N` out
of a cyclic `R`-module, which is exactly the specialization map `L_ξ → L_η` with its `R(X)`-
semilinearity. The two coordinates then differ by a unit of `R`, and `Ring.ordFrac_le_smul`
in both directions gives the equality of orders.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02SF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02SF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01X5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01X5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02MD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02MD)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### Specialization of stalks of a presheaf of modules -/

/-- Specialization of stalks of a presheaf of modules is semilinear over specialization of
stalks of its presheaf of rings. -/
theorem stalkSpecializes_smul
    {T : TopCat.{u}} (R : T.Presheaf CommRingCat.{u})
    (M : PresheafOfModules.{u} (R ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat.{u}))
    {x y : T} (h : x ⤳ y) (r : R.stalk y)
    (m : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) M.presheaf y) :
    TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes M.presheaf h (r • m) =
      TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes R h r •
        TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes M.presheaf h m := by
  obtain ⟨U, hyU, r₀, rfl⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq R r
  obtain ⟨V, hyV, m₀, rfl⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq M.presheaf m
  let W : Opens T := U ⊓ V
  have hyW : y ∈ W := ⟨hyU, hyV⟩
  have hxW : x ∈ W := ⟨h.mem_open U.isOpen hyU, h.mem_open V.isOpen hyV⟩
  have hWU : W ≤ U := by change U ⊓ V ≤ U; exact inf_le_left
  have hWV : W ≤ V := by change U ⊓ V ≤ V; exact inf_le_right
  let rW : R.obj (Opposite.op W) := R.map (homOfLE hWU).op r₀
  let m₀' : M.obj (Opposite.op V) := Eq.mp (M.presheaf_obj_coe (Opposite.op V)) m₀
  let mW : M.obj (Opposite.op W) := (M.map (homOfLE hWV).op).hom m₀'
  have hmW : (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op).hom m₀ = mW := by
    cases M.presheaf_obj_coe (Opposite.op V)
    rfl
  have hgy : TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf W y hyW (rW • mW) =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ R W y hyW rW • TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf W y hyW mW :=
    PresheafOfModules.germ_smul M y W hyW rW mW
  have hgx : TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf W x hxW (rW • mW) =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ R W x hxW rW • TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf W x hxW mW :=
    PresheafOfModules.germ_smul M x W hxW rW mW
  have hresR : TopCat.Presheaf.germ R W y hyW rW = TopCat.Presheaf.germ R U y hyU r₀ :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply R (homOfLE hWU) y hyW r₀
  have hresM : TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf W y hyW mW =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf V y hyV m₀ := by
    rw [← hmW]
    exact TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply M.presheaf (homOfLE hWV) y hyW m₀
  have hspecM (z : M.presheaf.obj (Opposite.op W)) :
      TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes M.presheaf h
          (TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf W y hyW z) =
        TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf W x hxW z := by
    change (TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf W y hyW ≫
      TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes M.presheaf h) z = _
    rw [TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes]
  have hspecR (z : R.obj (Opposite.op W)) :
      TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes R h (TopCat.Presheaf.germ R W y hyW z) =
        TopCat.Presheaf.germ R W x hxW z := by
    change (TopCat.Presheaf.germ R W y hyW ≫ TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes R h) z = _
    rw [TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes]
  calc TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes M.presheaf h
        (TopCat.Presheaf.germ R U y hyU r₀ • TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf V y hyV m₀)
      = TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes M.presheaf h
          (TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf W y hyW (rW • mW)) := by
        rw [hgy, hresR, hresM]
    _ = TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf W x hxW (rW • mW) := hspecM _
    _ = TopCat.Presheaf.germ R W x hxW rW •
          TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf W x hxW mW := hgx
    _ = TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes R h (TopCat.Presheaf.germ R U y hyU r₀) •
          TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes M.presheaf h
            (TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.presheaf V y hyV m₀) := by
        rw [← hresR, ← hresM, hspecR rW, hspecM mW]

/-! ### Independence of the order from the generator -/

/-- Two coordinates of one vector with respect to two generators of a cyclic module have the
same order: the generators differ by a unit of the base ring, so the coordinates differ by a
unit of the base ring too. -/
theorem ordFrac_eq_of_coordinates
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsDomain R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [Ring.KrullDimLE 1 R]
    {K : Type u} [Field K] [Algebra R K] [IsFractionRing R K]
    {M : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    {N : Type u} [AddCommGroup N] [Module K N]
    (f : M →ₛₗ[algebraMap R K] N)
    (m m' : M) (hspan : Submodule.span R ({m} : Set M) = ⊤)
    (hspan' : Submodule.span R ({m'} : Set M) = ⊤)
    (hm : f m ≠ 0) (hm' : f m' ≠ 0)
    (n : N) (a b : K) (ha : n = a • f m) (hb : n = b • f m') :
    Ring.ordFrac R a = Ring.ordFrac R b := by
  have key : ∀ (m m' : M) (a b : K), Submodule.span R ({m} : Set M) = ⊤ → f m ≠ 0 → f m' ≠ 0 →
      a • f m = b • f m' → Ring.ordFrac R b ≤ Ring.ordFrac R a := by
    intro m m' a b hspan hm hm' h
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_singleton.mp (by simp [hspan] : m' ∈ Submodule.span R {m})
    have hr0 : r ≠ 0 := by
      rintro rfl
      exact hm' (by simp [← hr])
    have hcoeff : a = b * algebraMap R K r := by
      apply smul_left_injective K hm
      dsimp only
      rw [h, ← hr, f.map_smulₛₗ, smul_smul]
    rw [hcoeff]
    simpa [Algebra.smul_def, mul_comm] using
      (Ring.ordFrac_le_smul (R := R) (K := K) (S := R) r (by simpa) b)
  exact le_antisymm (key m' m b a hspan' hm' hm (hb.symm.trans ha))
    (key m m' a b hspan hm hm' (ha.symm.trans hb))

/-! ### Stalks of a sheaf of modules trivialized by a section -/

/-- If multiplication by a section `s` of `L` over `U` is surjective onto the sections of `L`
over every smaller open set, then the germ of `s` generates the stalk of `L` at every point of
`U`. -/
theorem span_germ_eq_top_of_surjective_smul
    (X : Scheme.{u}) (L : X.Modules) (U : X.Opens) (s : L.val.obj (op U))
    (hsurj : ∀ (W : X.Opens) (hWU : W ≤ U), Function.Surjective
      (fun r : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W) => r • (L.val.map (homOfLE hWU).op).hom s))
    (x : X) (hx : x ∈ U) :
    letI : Module (X.presheaf.stalk x)
        (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) L.val.presheaf x) :=
      PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
        (R := X.presheaf) L.val x
    Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk x)
      {TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf U x hx s} = ⊤ := by
  classical
  let : Module (X.presheaf.stalk x)
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) L.val.presheaf x) :=
    PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
      (R := X.presheaf) L.val x
  change Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk x)
    {TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf U x hx s} = ⊤
  refine le_antisymm le_top fun z _ => ?_
  obtain ⟨V, hV, v, hv⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq L.val.presheaf z
  let W : X.Opens := U ⊓ V
  have hWU : W ≤ U := inf_le_left
  have hWV : W ≤ V := inf_le_right
  have hxW : x ∈ W := ⟨hx, hV⟩
  let sW : L.val.obj (op W) := (L.val.map (homOfLE hWU).op).hom s
  let vW : L.val.obj (op W) := (L.val.map (homOfLE hWV).op).hom v
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hsurj W hWU vW
  have hcsm : c • sW = vW := hc
  let cComm : X.presheaf.obj (op W) := c
  have hsm : TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf W x hxW (c • sW) =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ X.presheaf W x hxW cComm •
        TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf W x hxW sW :=
    PresheafOfModules.germ_smul L.val x W hxW cComm sW
  have hres : TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf W x hxW sW =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf U x hx s :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply L.val.presheaf (homOfLE hWU) x hxW s
  have hresv : TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf W x hxW vW =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf V x hV v :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply L.val.presheaf (homOfLE hWV) x hxW v
  have hz : z = TopCat.Presheaf.germ X.presheaf W x hxW cComm •
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf U x hx s := by
    rw [← hres, ← hsm, hcsm, hresv, hv]
  rw [hz]
  exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span (Set.mem_singleton _))

/-- If multiplication by a section `s` of `L` over `U` is injective on the sections of the
structure sheaf over every smaller open set, then the germ of `s` at every point of `U` is
nonzero. -/
theorem germ_ne_zero_of_injective_smul
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsIntegral X] (L : X.Modules) (U : X.Opens) (s : L.val.obj (op U))
    (hinj : ∀ (W : X.Opens) (hWU : W ≤ U), Function.Injective
      (fun r : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W) => r • (L.val.map (homOfLE hWU).op).hom s))
    (x : X) (hx : x ∈ U) :
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf U x hx s ≠ 0 := by
  classical
  intro hzero
  have hzero' : TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf U x hx s =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf U x hx 0 := by
    rw [hzero, map_zero]
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, iWU, iWU', heq⟩ :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ_eq L.val.presheaf x hx hx s 0 hzero'
  rw [Subsingleton.elim iWU' iWU, map_zero] at heq
  have : Nonempty W := ⟨x, hxW⟩
  have hdom : IsDomain Γ(X, W) := IsIntegral.component_integral W
  have hone : (1 : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)) = 0 := by
    refine hinj W iWU.le ?_
    change (1 : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)) •
        (L.val.map (homOfLE (iWU.le : W ≤ U)).op).hom s =
      (0 : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)) •
        (L.val.map (homOfLE (iWU.le : W ≤ U)).op).hom s
    rw [one_smul, zero_smul, Subsingleton.elim (homOfLE (iWU.le : W ≤ U)) iWU]
    exact heq
  exact one_ne_zero (α := Γ(X, W)) hone

/-! ### The order of vanishing -/

/-- **Stacks 02SF, the content of the definition.** Let `X` be a locally Noetherian integral
scheme, `L` a sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules and `ξ` a point of codimension one. Let `g` generate the
stalk `L_ξ`, with nonzero image generating the stalk `L_η` at the generic point. Then a
meromorphic section `t` of `L` — a global section of the constant generic-stalk module sheaf —
has a coordinate with respect to every generator of `L_ξ`, and the order of that coordinate in
`𝒪_{X, ξ}` is one and the same integer whatever generator is used. -/
theorem nonempty_orderOfVanishingData
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsIntegral X] (L : X.Modules)
    (ξ : X) (hξ : Order.coheight ξ = 1)
    (t : (constantGenericStalkModuleSheaf X L).val.obj (op ⊤)) :
    letI : Module (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) (L.presheaf.stalk ξ) :=
      PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
        (R := X.presheaf) L.val ξ
    letI : Module (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X))
        (L.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) :=
      PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
        (R := X.presheaf) L.val (genericPoint X)
    letI : Module X.functionField (L.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) :=
      PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
        (R := X.presheaf) L.val (genericPoint X)
    ∀ g : L.presheaf.stalk ξ,
      Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) {g} = ⊤ →
      Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X))
        {(L.presheaf.stalkSpecializes
          ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial)) g} = ⊤ →
      (L.presheaf.stalkSpecializes ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial)) g ≠ 0 →
      Nonempty { d : ℤ //
        let R := X.presheaf.stalk ξ
        let K := X.functionField
        let isCoordinate := fun (m : L.presheaf.stalk ξ) (a : K) =>
          t = constantGenericStalkModuleSection X L ⊤
            (a • (L.presheaf.stalkSpecializes
              ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial)) m)
        (∃ m : L.presheaf.stalk ξ,
          (Submodule.span R {m} = ⊤) ∧ (∃ a : K, isCoordinate m a)) ∧
        (∀ (m : L.presheaf.stalk ξ)
          (_ : Submodule.span R {m} = ⊤) (a : K),
          isCoordinate m a → d = X.ord a ξ) } := by
  classical
  intro gξ hspanξ hspanη hgηne
  let η : X := genericPoint X
  let hηξ : η ⤳ ξ := (genericPoint_spec X).specializes (by trivial)
  let : Module (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) (L.presheaf.stalk ξ) :=
    PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
      (R := X.presheaf) L.val ξ
  let : Module (X.presheaf.stalk η) (L.presheaf.stalk η) :=
    PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
      (R := X.presheaf) L.val η
  let : Module X.functionField (L.presheaf.stalk η) :=
    PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
      (R := X.presheaf) L.val η
  let : Module (X.presheaf.stalk η)
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) L.val.presheaf η) :=
    PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
      (R := X.presheaf) L.val η
  let : Module X.functionField
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) L.val.presheaf η) :=
    PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
      (R := X.presheaf) L.val η
  let : IsScalarTower (X.presheaf.stalk η) X.functionField
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) L.val.presheaf η) := by
    apply IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul
    intro r m
    simp [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra]
  let gη : L.presheaf.stalk η :=
    (TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hηξ) gξ
  change Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk η) ({gη} : Set (L.presheaf.stalk η)) = ⊤ at hspanη
  change gη ≠ 0 at hgηne
  have hspanηK : Submodule.span X.functionField ({gη} : Set (L.presheaf.stalk η)) = ⊤ := by
    refine le_antisymm le_top fun z _ => ?_
    have hzR : z ∈ Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk η) ({gη} : Set (L.presheaf.stalk η)) := by
      rw [hspanη]; exact Submodule.mem_top
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_singleton.mp hzR
    have hrK : z = algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk η) X.functionField r • gη :=
      hr.symm.trans (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul X.functionField r gη).symm
    rw [hrK]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span (Set.mem_singleton _))
  let f : L.presheaf.stalk ξ →ₛₗ[algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) X.functionField]
      L.presheaf.stalk η := {
    toFun := fun m => (ConcreteCategory.hom
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hηξ)) m
    map_add' := fun x y => (ConcreteCategory.hom
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hηξ)).map_add x y
    map_smul' := by
      intro r m
      let σR := TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes X.presheaf hηξ
      let σL := TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hηξ
      have hs := stalkSpecializes_smul X.presheaf L.val hηξ r m
      let : Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) (X.presheaf.stalk η) :=
        RingHom.toAlgebra (ConcreteCategory.hom σR)
      let : IsScalarTower (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) (X.presheaf.stalk η) X.functionField :=
        IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq (by
          intro x
          simp [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra, σR])
      have hcomp : algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) X.functionField r =
          algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk η) X.functionField ((ConcreteCategory.hom σR) r) := by
        simp [RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra, σR]
      calc
        (ConcreteCategory.hom σL) (r • m) = (ConcreteCategory.hom σR) r •
            (ConcreteCategory.hom σL) m := hs
        _ = algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk η) X.functionField ((ConcreteCategory.hom σR) r) •
            (ConcreteCategory.hom σL) m :=
          (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul X.functionField ((ConcreteCategory.hom σR) r)
            ((ConcreteCategory.hom σL) m)).symm
        _ = algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) X.functionField r •
            (ConcreteCategory.hom σL) m :=
          congrArg (fun c : X.functionField => c • (ConcreteCategory.hom σL) m) hcomp.symm }
  have hgη : f gξ = gη := rfl
  obtain ⟨mη, hmη, hmη_unique⟩ := exists_unique_eq_constantGenericStalkModuleSection X L t
  have hmemη : mη ∈ Submodule.span X.functionField ({gη} : Set (L.presheaf.stalk η)) := by
    rw [hspanηK]; exact Submodule.mem_top
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_singleton.mp hmemη
  have ha' : mη = a • gη := ha.symm
  have hcoordBase : t = constantGenericStalkModuleSection X L ⊤
      (a • ((ConcreteCategory.hom
        (TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hηξ)) gξ)) := by
    rw [hmη, ha']
    rfl
  have hmapInjective : Function.Injective
      (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) X.functionField) := IsFractionRing.injective _ _
  have hgξne : gξ ≠ 0 := by
    intro hg
    apply hgηne
    change (ConcreteCategory.hom
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hηξ)) gξ = 0
    rw [hg]
    exact map_zero f
  have hfm_ne (m : L.presheaf.stalk ξ)
      (hm : Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) ({m} : Set (L.presheaf.stalk ξ)) = ⊤) :
      f m ≠ 0 := by
    intro hzero
    have hmem : m ∈ Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) ({gξ} : Set (L.presheaf.stalk ξ)) := by
      rw [hspanξ]; exact Submodule.mem_top
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_singleton.mp hmem
    have hmap : f m = algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) X.functionField r • gη := by
      calc
        f m = f (r • gξ) := congrArg f hr.symm
        _ = algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) X.functionField r • f gξ := f.map_smulₛₗ r gξ
        _ = algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) X.functionField r • gη := by rw [hgη]
    rw [hzero] at hmap
    have hr0 : algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) X.functionField r = 0 :=
      (smul_eq_zero.mp hmap.symm).resolve_right hgηne
    have hm0 : m = 0 := by
      have hrzero : r = 0 := hmapInjective (by simpa using hr0)
      calc
        m = r • gξ := hr.symm
        _ = 0 := by simp [hrzero]
    have hmemG : gξ ∈ Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk ξ)
        ({m} : Set (L.presheaf.stalk ξ)) := by
      rw [hm]; exact Submodule.mem_top
    rw [hm0] at hmemG
    exact hgξne (by simpa using hmemG)
  refine ⟨⟨X.ord a ξ, ?_⟩⟩
  change (∃ m : L.presheaf.stalk ξ,
        (Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) {m} = ⊤) ∧
        ∃ b : X.functionField,
          t = constantGenericStalkModuleSection X L ⊤
            (b • ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hηξ) m))) ∧
    ∀ (m : L.presheaf.stalk ξ)
      (_ : Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) {m} = ⊤) (b : X.functionField),
      t = constantGenericStalkModuleSection X L ⊤
            (b • ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hηξ) m)) →
        X.ord a ξ = X.ord b ξ
  refine ⟨⟨gξ, hspanξ, a, by simpa [f] using hcoordBase⟩, ?_⟩
  intro m hm b hb
  have hscalar := hmη_unique (b • (f m)) hb
  have hfm := hfm_ne m hm
  by_cases ha0 : a = 0
  · have hmη0 : mη = 0 := by rw [ha0, zero_smul] at ha'; exact ha'
    have hb0 : b = 0 := by
      have hprod : b • (f m) = 0 := by rw [← hscalar, hmη0]
      exact (smul_eq_zero.mp hprod).resolve_right hfm
    simp [ha0, hb0]
  · have hb0 : b ≠ 0 := by
      intro hbzero
      have hmη0 : mη = 0 := by simpa [hbzero] using hscalar
      have hbasezero : a • gη = 0 := by rw [← ha', hmη0]
      exact ha0 ((smul_eq_zero.mp hbasezero).resolve_right hgηne)
    have hchosen : mη = a • (f gξ) := by
      apply hmη_unique
      change t = constantGenericStalkModuleSection X L ⊤
        (a • ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hηξ) gξ))
      exact hcoordBase
    let : Ring.KrullDimLE 1 (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) :=
      AlgebraicGeometry.krullDimLE_of_coheight_le hξ.le
    have hfgξne : f gξ ≠ 0 := by rw [hgη]; exact hgηne
    have hsame := ordFrac_eq_of_coordinates
      (R := X.presheaf.stalk ξ) (K := X.functionField)
      (M := L.presheaf.stalk ξ) (N := L.presheaf.stalk η) f gξ m
      hspanξ hm hfgξne hfm mη a b hchosen hscalar
    have hhom : X.ordHom ξ hξ a = X.ordHom ξ hξ b := hsame
    have hbOrd := (X.ord_eq_iff hξ hb0).mp rfl
    refine (X.ord_eq_iff hξ ha0).2 ?_
    rw [hhom]
    exact hbOrd

/-- **Stacks 02SF for a sheaf trivialized near `ξ`.** If multiplication by a section `s` over
an open set `U` containing `ξ` is bijective onto the sections of `L` over every smaller open
set — as it is for an invertible sheaf, by Tag 0B8M — then the order of vanishing along `ξ` is
defined. -/
theorem nonempty_orderOfVanishingData_of_bijective_smul
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsIntegral X] (L : X.Modules)
    (ξ : X) (hξ : Order.coheight ξ = 1)
    (U : X.Opens) (hξU : ξ ∈ U) (s : L.val.obj (op U))
    (hbij : ∀ (W : X.Opens) (hWU : W ≤ U), Function.Bijective
      (fun r : X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W) => r • (L.val.map (homOfLE hWU).op).hom s))
    (t : (constantGenericStalkModuleSheaf X L).val.obj (op ⊤)) :
    Nonempty { d : ℤ //
      let R := X.presheaf.stalk ξ
      let K := X.functionField
      letI : Module R (L.presheaf.stalk ξ) :=
        PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
          (R := X.presheaf) L.val ξ
      letI : Module K (L.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) :=
        PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
          (R := X.presheaf) L.val (genericPoint X)
      let isCoordinate := fun (m : L.presheaf.stalk ξ) (a : K) =>
        t = constantGenericStalkModuleSection X L ⊤
          (a • (L.presheaf.stalkSpecializes
            ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial)) m)
      (∃ m : L.presheaf.stalk ξ,
        (Submodule.span R {m} = ⊤) ∧ (∃ a : K, isCoordinate m a)) ∧
      (∀ (m : L.presheaf.stalk ξ)
        (_ : Submodule.span R {m} = ⊤) (a : K),
        isCoordinate m a → d = X.ord a ξ) } := by
  classical
  let η : X := genericPoint X
  have hηU : η ∈ U :=
    ((genericPoint_spec X).mem_open_set_iff U.isOpen).2 ⟨ξ, ⟨Set.mem_univ _, hξU⟩⟩
  let hηξ : η ⤳ ξ := (genericPoint_spec X).specializes (by trivial)
  let : Module (X.presheaf.stalk ξ)
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) L.val.presheaf ξ) :=
    PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
      (R := X.presheaf) L.val ξ
  let : Module (X.presheaf.stalk η)
      (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) L.val.presheaf η) :=
    PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
      (R := X.presheaf) L.val η
  let g : TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := Ab.{u}) L.val.presheaf ξ :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf U ξ hξU s
  have hspec : (TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hηξ) g =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ L.val.presheaf U η hηU s :=
    congrArg (fun φ => (ConcreteCategory.hom φ) s)
      (TopCat.Presheaf.germ_stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hξU hηξ)
  have hspanξ : Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) {g} = ⊤ :=
    span_germ_eq_top_of_surjective_smul X L U s (fun W hWU => (hbij W hWU).2) ξ hξU
  have hspanη : Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk η)
      {(TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hηξ) g} = ⊤ := by
    rw [hspec]
    exact span_germ_eq_top_of_surjective_smul X L U s (fun W hWU => (hbij W hWU).2) η hηU
  have hgηne : (TopCat.Presheaf.stalkSpecializes L.val.presheaf hηξ) g ≠ 0 := by
    rw [hspec]
    exact germ_ne_zero_of_injective_smul X L U s (fun W hWU => (hbij W hWU).1) η hηU
  exact nonempty_orderOfVanishingData X L ξ hξ t g hspanξ hspanη hgηne

/-- **Stacks 02SF.** The order of vanishing of a meromorphic section along a prime divisor,
together with its characterization by the order of a coordinate with respect to any generator
of the stalk. A choice of the data provided by
`AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_orderOfVanishingData`. -/
def orderOfVanishingData
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsIntegral X] (L : X.Modules)
    (ξ : X) (hξ : Order.coheight ξ = 1)
    (t : (constantGenericStalkModuleSheaf X L).val.obj (op ⊤)) :
    letI : Module (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) (L.presheaf.stalk ξ) :=
      PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
        (R := X.presheaf) L.val ξ
    letI : Module (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X))
        (L.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) :=
      PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
        (R := X.presheaf) L.val (genericPoint X)
    letI : Module X.functionField (L.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) :=
      PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
        (R := X.presheaf) L.val (genericPoint X)
    ∀ g : L.presheaf.stalk ξ,
      Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) {g} = ⊤ →
      Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X))
        {(L.presheaf.stalkSpecializes
          ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial)) g} = ⊤ →
      (L.presheaf.stalkSpecializes ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial)) g ≠ 0 →
      { d : ℤ //
        let R := X.presheaf.stalk ξ
        let K := X.functionField
        let isCoordinate := fun (m : L.presheaf.stalk ξ) (a : K) =>
          t = constantGenericStalkModuleSection X L ⊤
            (a • (L.presheaf.stalkSpecializes
              ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial)) m)
        (∃ m : L.presheaf.stalk ξ,
          (Submodule.span R {m} = ⊤) ∧ (∃ a : K, isCoordinate m a)) ∧
        (∀ (m : L.presheaf.stalk ξ)
          (_ : Submodule.span R {m} = ⊤) (a : K),
          isCoordinate m a → d = X.ord a ξ) } := by
  intro g h1 h2 h3
  exact Classical.choice (nonempty_orderOfVanishingData X L ξ hξ t g h1 h2 h3)

/-- **Stacks 02SF.** The order of vanishing along `ξ` of a meromorphic section `t` of `L`,
given a generator of the stalk `L_ξ` whose image at the generic point is a nonzero generator
of `L_η`. It is characterized by `AlgebraicGeometry.orderOfVanishingData`: it is the order of
the coordinate of `t` with respect to any generator of `L_ξ`. -/
def orderOfVanishing
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsIntegral X] (L : X.Modules)
    (ξ : X) (hξ : Order.coheight ξ = 1)
    (t : (constantGenericStalkModuleSheaf X L).val.obj (op ⊤)) :
    letI : Module (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) (L.presheaf.stalk ξ) :=
      PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
        (R := X.presheaf) L.val ξ
    letI : Module (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X))
        (L.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X)) :=
      PresheafOfModules.instModuleCarrierStalkCommRingCatCarrierAbPresheafOpensCarrier
        (R := X.presheaf) L.val (genericPoint X)
    ∀ g : L.presheaf.stalk ξ,
      Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk ξ) {g} = ⊤ →
      Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk (genericPoint X))
        {(L.presheaf.stalkSpecializes
          ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial)) g} = ⊤ →
      (L.presheaf.stalkSpecializes ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes trivial)) g ≠ 0 →
      ℤ := by
  intro g h1 h2 h3
  exact (orderOfVanishingData X L ξ hξ t g h1 h2 h3).val

